ist while the other is placed on the knee. [The arhat] sits, legs crossed [as if] ten thousand years were a day. [The arhat] has a slightly broad face, and an uneven skull that resembles peaks. If one asks about the meaning of the dharma, [the arhat responds with] two eyebrows covering cheeks.\nInscribed by Hyakunen\nInscription Text\/Poem\nTranslation: He reached Nirvana. And preaching it, his life has been in a dream.\nWritten by Chokuny\u016b\nSignature: \u666f\u5e74\u5c71\u4eba","makers":[{"name":"Imao Keinen \u4eca\u5c3e\u666f\u5e74","risdAffiliation":null,"years":"1845\u20131924, b. in Kyoto, Japan","nationality":["Japanese"],"nationalityModifiers":null,"role":null,"attribution_type":null},{"name":"Tanomura Chokuny\u016b \u7530\u80fd\u6751\u76f4\u5165","risdAffiliation":null,"years":"1814-1907, b. in \u014cita","nationality":["Japanese"],"nationalityModifiers":null,"role":null,"attribution_type":null},{"name":"Suzuki Hyakunen \u9234\u6728\u767e\u5e74","risdAffiliation":null,"years":"worked in Japan","nationality":["Japanese"],"nationalityModifiers":null,"role":null,"attribution_type":null}],"medium":["Hanging scroll","Ink and color on fabric"],"mediumTechnique":"","objectNumber":"2023.111.1","onView":false,"place":"Place Made: Japan","primaryMaker":"Tanomura Chokuny\u016b \u7530\u80fd\u6751\u76f4\u5165","publicDomain":false,"recentAcquisition":false,"referenceNumber":"","relatedObjects":["https:\/\/risdmuseum.org\/api\/v1\/collection?id=1636576"],"state":"","support":[],"technique":["Hanging scroll","Ink and color on fabric"],"title":"Arhats in Landscape","type":["Paintings"],"url":"https:\/\/risdmuseum.org\/art-design\/collection\/arhats-landscape-20231111"},{"id":"1213521","collection":"","credit":"Gift of Andrea Mozarowski and women of Mozhary, Ukraine","culture":"Ukrainian","dating":"","datingYearFrom":"1860","datingYearTo":"1899","description":"\u003Cp\u003ERushnyk (ritual towel) or hanging\u003C\/p\u003E\n","dimensions":"Width: 29.2 cm (11 1\/2 inches)",